<BaseLayout hreflang={false}
  title="Shipping from China to Finland: Cost, Transit & 25.5% VAT"
  description="China to Finland freight: 35–45-day sea via the northern range plus a Baltic feeder to Helsinki/Kotka, 25.5% VAT, EU duty, EORI and the winter ice season."
  canonical={pageUrl}
  ogType="article"
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb
        items={[
          { label: 'Europe', href: '/europe/' },
          { label: 'Shipping from China to Finland' },
        ]}
      />
      <span class="badge badge--amber">September 2026 updated</span>
      <h1>Shipping from China to Finland: Helsinki FIHEL &amp; Kotka FIKTK feeders, 25.5% VAT, 1524mm gauge &amp; the Baltic ice season</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A one-page freight brief for importers moving cargo from Shanghai, Ningbo-Zhoushan, Shenzhen
        and the wider China origin set to Helsinki, Kotka and the Finnish market — with the Baltic-feeder
        geography, the roughly 35–45-day sea window via the northern range, the 22–28-day rail-plus-short-sea
        alternative, EU common duty plus 25.5% VAT, the 1524mm broad-gauge rail wall, the winter ice season,
        the EUR currency advantage, the EORI gate, and the hidden destination charges that shape the Finnish
        landed cost.
