      Małaszewicze (Poland); Finland's own 1524 mm gauge adds a further break at the Finnish border, which is
      why no through train rolls into Finland.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>4. Sea vs rail vs air: Finland's true door-to-door decision</h2>
      <p>
        Finland's two ports are both feeder terminals, so the honest comparison is <strong>door-to-door,
        not port-to-port</strong> — and it is really a sea-versus-air decision with a narrow rail hybrid in
        the middle. Roughly <strong>35–45 days</strong> by sea (32–40 to the northern range plus a ~3–5-day
        feeder) against roughly <strong>22–28 days</strong> by a rail-plus-short-sea hybrid, against air,
        whose verified rate and transit the snapshot does not publish.
      </p>

