      The origin side is the familiar China port hierarchy: Shanghai and Ningbo-Zhoushan anchor the
      East China ocean services, while Shenzhen and Guangzhou cover South China and Qingdao, Tianjin
      and Xiamen provide northern/southeast alternatives. The destination side is Finland's two feeder
      ports: <strong>Helsinki (FIHEL)</strong> on the Gulf of Finland is the capital gate and largest
      container port, while <strong>Kotka (FIKTK)</strong>, part of the merged Port of HaminaKotka, is
      Finland's largest general-cargo port for the eastern Gulf of Finland. Neither is a deep-sea mainline
      call — the ~3–5-day Baltic feeder is what the northern-range ocean quote omits.
    </p>

